* cascade_erp.dts -- Cascade Precision Mfg ERP: x64base DBF environment
* System bundle (owner ruling 2026-08-10): everything Cascade lives under
* dottalkpp/data/systems/cascade_erp/. This script sets the slots, opens a
* sane working set, and attaches indexes where they exist.
*
* Run from the data root (datarun.ps1 cwd):  DOTSCRIPT systems/cascade_erp/scripts/cascade_erp.dts
* Schema + tag orders: systems/cascade_erp/schema/CASCADE_ERP.dtgraph (generated)
* (.dtschema is the engine WORKSPACE SAVE/LOAD snapshot format -- save your
*  open state with WORKSPACE SAVE <name> after running this script)
* Physical index build (once, or after re-mirror): cascade_erp_build_indexes.dts
* SQLite twin: cascade_sql.dts

SET TALK ON
ECHO === CASCADE ERP (x64base DBF side) ===

* --- environment: point every slot into the bundle -----------------------
SET PATH DBF SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/DBF
SET PATH INDEXES SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/INDEXES
SET PATH LMDB SYSTEMS/CASCADE_ERP/LMDB

* --- working set: one table per module spine -----------------------------
* Area 1: Items (inventory hub -- most-referenced parent, 8 inbound FKs)
SELECT 1
USE CASCADE_Items
* Area 2: Vendors (procurement parent)
SELECT 2
USE CASCADE_Vendors
* Area 3: Customers (sales parent)
SELECT 3
USE CASCADE_Customers
* Area 4: Sales_Orders (order-to-cash spine)
SELECT 4
USE CASCADE_Sales_Orders
* Area 5: Purchase_Orders (procure-to-pay spine)
SELECT 5
USE CASCADE_Purchase_Orders
* Area 6: Work_Orders (plan-to-produce spine)
SELECT 6
USE CASCADE_Work_Orders
* Area 7: GL_Journal (close-to-report spine)
SELECT 7
USE CASCADE_GL_Journal

* --- indexes: attach where built ----------------------------------------
* Until cascade_erp_build_indexes.dts has run, these SET INDEX lines will
* report not-found; that is expected, not an error in this script.
SELECT 1
SET INDEX TO CASCADE_Items.cdx
SET ORDER TO TAG ITEM_ID
SELECT 4
SET INDEX TO CASCADE_Sales_Orders.cdx
SET ORDER TO TAG SO_ID

* --- walker #2 demo: the house SELECT (second SELECT optional) -----------
* SQLSEL reads OPEN DBF work areas, so it queries a table this script opened
* (Sales_Orders, area 4). Expected: exactly one row, SO 1 (measured
* 2026-08-10). The set answer beside the positional one.
SQLSEL SO_ID, CUSTOMER_ID, STATUS FROM CASCADE_Sales_Orders WHERE SO_ID = 1

* --- prove the environment, do not just assert it ------------------------
SELECT 1
LIST STATUS
ECHO === CASCADE x64base environment ready: 7 areas open ===
